@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home";
}

<p class="eyebrow">Code sample</p>
<h1>Claims Portal</h1>
<p class="lead">
    A small weekly benefit claims app built with ASP.NET Core MVC, a REST API, EF Core on SQL Server
    and the transactional outbox pattern. Every page is built to WCAG 2.1 AA and works without JavaScript.
</p>

<div class="hero__actions">
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/claims/new">File a weekly claim</a>
    <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/claims">See all claims</a>
</div>

<h2>What to look at</h2>
<ul class="card-grid" role="list">
    <li class="card">
        <h3 class="card__title">Accessible server side validation</h3>
        <p>Errors come back in a focused summary that links to each field, with <code>aria-invalid</code> and <code>aria-describedby</code> added by a custom tag helper.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
        <h3 class="card__title">REST API</h3>
        <p>Paging, sorting and validation errors as ProblemDetails. See the <a href="/openapi/v1.json">OpenAPI document</a>.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
        <h3 class="card__title">Integration ready</h3>
        <p>Each claim writes an outbox message in the same transaction, and a background worker publishes it with retries.</p>
    </li>
</ul>
